<h2>
  <label class="section-header">
    <input type="checkbox" class="section-check" data-section="3">
    <span>3. The --debug Flag — Multi-Flag in One Argument</span>
    <span class="section-label">(read)</span>
  </label>
</h2>

<p><code>--debug</code> is a single option that takes a string of flag characters, each enabling a different <code>Modes.debug_X</code> boolean. The handler iterates over every character — <span class="filepath">readsb.c:2306</span>:</p>

<pre><span class="kw">case</span> OptDebug:
    <span class="kw">for</span> (<span class="kw">int</span> j = <span class="num">0</span>; arg[j]; j++) {
        <span class="kw">switch</span> (arg[j]) {
            <span class="kw">case</span> <span class="str">'n'</span>: Modes.debug_net = <span class="num">1</span>;            <span class="kw">break</span>;
            <span class="kw">case</span> <span class="str">'N'</span>: Modes.debug_nextra = <span class="num">1</span>;         <span class="kw">break</span>;
            <span class="kw">case</span> <span class="str">'P'</span>: Modes.debug_cpr = <span class="num">1</span>;            <span class="kw">break</span>;
            <span class="kw">case</span> <span class="str">'S'</span>: Modes.debug_speed_check = <span class="num">1</span>;   <span class="kw">break</span>;
            <span class="kw">case</span> <span class="str">'G'</span>: Modes.debug_garbage = <span class="num">1</span>;        <span class="kw">break</span>;
            <span class="kw">case</span> <span class="str">'K'</span>: Modes.debug_sampleCounter = <span class="num">1</span>;  <span class="kw">break</span>;
            <span class="kw">case</span> <span class="str">'R'</span>: Modes.debug_receiver = <span class="num">1</span>;       <span class="kw">break</span>;
            <span class="cm">/* ... more ... */</span>
        }
    }
    <span class="kw">break</span>;</pre>

<p>So <code>--debug nPS</code> enables net, CPR, and speed-check debug simultaneously with one flag. You can combine any characters in any order.</p>

