<h2>
  <label class="section-header">
    <input type="checkbox" class="section-check" data-section="4">
    <span>4. The --devel Flag — Runtime Debugging Strings</span>
    <span class="section-label">(read)</span>
  </label>
</h2>

<p><code>--devel</code> is a more powerful but undocumented developer flag. It accepts a string that is tokenized and parsed at runtime. Unlike <code>--debug</code> characters, devel modes can carry parameters — <span class="filepath">readsb.c:2149</span>:</p>

<pre><span class="kw">case</span> OptDevel:
    <span class="cm">// tokenize the string by spaces or '='</span>
    n = tokenize(arg, token, maxTokens);

    <span class="kw">if</span> (n >= <span class="num">2</span> &amp;&amp; !strcmp(token[<span class="num">0</span>], <span class="str">"lastStatus"</span>)) {
        Modes.debug_lastStatus = atoi(token[<span class="num">1</span>]);
        fprintf(stderr, <span class="str">"lastStatus: %d\n"</span>, Modes.debug_lastStatus);
    }
    <span class="cm">/* ... many more string comparisons ... */</span>

    <span class="kw">case</span> <span class="str">'n'</span>: Modes.debug_net = <span class="num">1</span>; <span class="kw">break</span>;  <span class="cm">// single-char fallthrough</span>
    <span class="kw">case</span> <span class="str">'f'</span>: Modes.debug_flush = <span class="num">1</span>; <span class="kw">break</span>;
    <span class="kw">case</span> <span class="str">'g'</span>: Modes.debug_gps = <span class="num">1</span>; <span class="kw">break</span>;
    <span class="kw">case</span> <span class="str">'z'</span>: Modes.debug_zstd = <span class="num">1</span>; <span class="kw">break</span>;
    <span class="cm">/* ... */</span></pre>

<p>Example usage: <code>--devel lastStatus=2</code> or <code>--devel planefinder</code>. Because the option help says "see source for options", these are developer-only escape hatches — search <code>readsb.c</code> around line 2149 for the current list.</p>

<div class="callout warn">
  <strong>--devel can be specified multiple times.</strong> Each invocation adds more debug flags. The option table marks it without <code>OPTION_HIDDEN</code> in readsb (but not in viewadsb), so it shows up in <code>--help</code> for readsb.
</div>

